\ Interpreter-free (`--interpreter-fallback=false`) build of the standalone
\ lint driver. The build now SUCCEEDS: the lexer / lint row-variable words
\ -- `(lexer-step)`, `(try-rules)`, `(lint-rule-with-context)` -- all compile,
\ the last one through the interpreter-free runtime-selected dispatch over a
\ symbolic row (`check>> call`). This is a build-only fixture: the binary is not
\ run yet, because the lint rules live in module-private mutable-map state
\ serialized into the runtime image, and a quotation value decoded from that
\ image still carries a null `code_ptr` (it is never discovered for compilation,
\ serializes with the sentinel quotation_id, and the loader does not attach a
\ compiled function), so a `check>> call` of an image-decoded rule traps at
\ runtime. Attaching compiled `code_ptr`s to runtime-image quotation values is
\ separate follow-up work; once it lands this flips to a run fixture matching
\ interpreted `1z lint`.
use "lint" ;
use "lint-rules" ;
{ "tests/fixtures/lint/unused-import.1z" } run-lint [ 0 ] [ 1 ] if sys-exit
